    <briefdescription>
<para>Specialisation of <computeroutput><ref refid="class_d_mat_lin_alg" kindref="compound">DMatLinAlg</ref></computeroutput> for <computeroutput>ARingZZpFlint</computeroutput> dense matrices, routing rank / determinant / kernel / solve / inverse calls to FLINT&apos;s <computeroutput>nmod_mat_*</computeroutput> routines. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="class_d_mat" kindref="compound">DMat</ref>&lt;ARingZZpFlint&gt;</computeroutput> already wraps an <computeroutput>nmod_mat_t</computeroutput>, so the linear-algebra layer just hands the underlying FLINT matrix to the right <computeroutput>nmod_mat_*</computeroutput> entry point and converts the result back. Gives word-prime <computeroutput>Z/p</computeroutput> matrices the same FLINT speed-up the FFPACK specialisation provides for primes that fit in a FFPACK word. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
